OL,3,ABurnham insists 'no confusion at all'
OL,4,Aover his Brexit position
OL,5,
OL,6,FAndy Burnham has insisted there is "no
OL,7,Fconfusion" over his position on the
OL,8,FEuropean Union, as he criticised the
OL,9,FUK's current deal with the bloc.
OL,11,FThe prime minister said it was his
OL,12,F"responsibility" to improve the deal,
OL,13,Fwhich was ratified in 2020, at a summit
OL,14,Fin Brussels next month.
OL,16,FHe denied he had shifted his stance
OL,17,Fsince the Makerfield by-election when
OL,18,Fhe promised not to "re-run" the Brexit
OL,19,Fdebate. Earlier this week, he suggested
OL,20,Fhe could call a referendum on the UK
OL,21,Freturning to EU freedom of movement,
OL,22,Fbefore No10 appeared to backtrack.
OL,23,APub: 28-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
